A||N||12||Monkeyman||Bikers??||||6||
Z||000000||Monkeyman||03-19-2001||01:08 PM||||Anybody in the Midwest/Great Lakes area ride a bike?  It doesn't matter if it's a new Fatboy (one of my personal faves) or an old, rusty Honda.  Everyone's a brother/sister when they're on 2 wheels.  I just bought an '86 Suzuki Intruder and might like to go riding with someone else.  No overnighters (I don't have the time).  Just a few easy day trips.||||reg||6
Z||000001||fierospeeder||03-19-2001||02:34 PM||||I have a 83 honda nighthawk 550.<BR>Im planning on purchasing a new tire for my rear and new pads and shoes.<P>The longest i have riden was 140 miles total going to leland,illinois, down i-55 then west on route 80 and north on route 23.  Went to look at a guy who owned a small vw beetle junkyard.  The ride was great because its all farm and is there is no traffic.  I did see other bikers on the route and did the usual hand wave.<P>Besides that, i ride through the woods where i live, less traffic and the curves are sweet.||||reg||1
Z||000002||DaRkLoRD||03-19-2001||03:09 PM||||My dad's really into bikes, he has a Honda Silverwing, and wants to buy a Goldwing. He seems to think Fieros are unsafe, yet when I asked him if I could get a Kawasaki Ninja, he immediatly went online and started showing me pictures and looking up prices etc.. go figure!<P>------------------<BR>  <A HREF="mailto:steve@fieroproject.com">steve@fieroproject.com</A>  <BR><A HREF="http://www.fieroproject.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fieroproject.com</A>||||reg||12
Z||000003||DRH||03-20-2001||12:38 AM||||I have an 82 Honda GL500I Silverwing I bought new in 84. I ride it to work and around the local countryside from time to time. It's not really comfortable enough for long trips. ||||reg||1
Z||000004||ChadMan||03-20-2001||01:06 PM||||I have an '82 Yamaha Maxim 750 that my uncle bought new, then sold to my best friend, who sold it to me.  It's reasonably fast, comfortable, and in great shape, but it's big and heavy and I sometimes miss my old CB350.<P>I'd be glad to ride with you sometime, Monkey, but Columbus to Wabash and back is kind of a long haul.<P>Silverwing...is that a touring bike with a 500cc V-twin?<p>[This message has been edited by ChadMan (edited 03-20-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000005||Monkeyman||03-20-2001||01:08 PM||||Chad--Next time I get down to the Middletown area, maybe we can go riding.  Hopefully, I'll be down there in the next month or 2.  I'll email you when something is finalized.<P>MM||||reg||1
Z||000006||DRH||03-20-2001||06:01 PM||||Chad,<P>The GL500 Silverwing is a lot like the CX500. It's a water cooled V twin with the V "sideways" (the heads stick out on either side of the tank). The one I have is a GL500I. The "I" stands for Interstate and it came with a fairing, removeable hard saddlebags and a small trunk you could interchange with the back seat. Kinda like a baby brother to the Goldwing (Actually uses the same fairing). <P>I'm not sure how they were classified... kinda small for touring... The "Interstate" badge implies more comfort than is really there for a long trip. The cylinder arrangement doesn't lend itself to having a good position for highway pegs. Pretty nice for short rides though. decent power (for 500cc on a 500+ lb bike)... a place to put stuff... 45 to 55 MPG depending on how much I punch it.<P>I think thay were made from 80 or 81 to 82, then bumped to a 650 in 83 and 84 before going the way of our Fieros.<P>David.||||reg||1
Z||000007||KnightRyder31||03-20-2001||06:35 PM||||Whats the fastest speed you guys have had a bike going???<P>||||reg||1
Z||000008||LarryB||03-20-2001||07:21 PM||||Approx. 125MPH on an '82 Honda CB900F.  Some yuppie scum in a BMW was looking for kicks so I took off. <BR>||||reg||1
Z||000009||fierospeeder||03-20-2001||08:04 PM||||The fastest ive gone was 100mph might have been more, this was at night going through the woods, without a helmet.  So im pretty much screwed if there was a deer, which i have seen before.<BR>Im not sure if it was windy or if it was my fairing making my frontend light, but the bike was shaking side to side, its like someone is trying to shake you off the bike.<P>Just rode my bike today, needed a new relay for my turnsignal, honda wants 40 bucks, and they cant get an aftermarket??   So im either going to look at a car parts store, ask the nighthawk forum, or be lucky enough to find one at the junkyard.  <P>I totally hate dealerships, the worst is probably honda-motorcycle, ford then GM. The guy was going through couple relays, mine has a "different plug" but the others were also 40 bucks, i got to see the "honda stockroom"||||reg||1
Z||000010||87ECO5||03-20-2001||09:52 PM||||Chad/Dave - wish I'd known you guys back when I had (and was "allowed" to have) crotch rockets ...    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif">||||reg||6
Z||000011||Songman||03-20-2001||10:10 PM||||I've got a 97 FatBoy but don't live up there. Always good to find someone to ride with though so I wish I did...<P>As far as fastest on a bike... Let me tell you, you get over about 80 on a Harley where you sit straight up and it is all you can do to hang on... Harleys are made to look good and sound good. You don't need to go fast for that. Slow down and enjoy the ride...<P>This pic is before the passing lights were added.<BR> <IMG SRC="http://dalehouston.com/harley.jpg"> <P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/songman_1.gif"> <BR><A HREF="http://members.home.com/tnfieros" TARGET=_blank>Tennessee Fiero Owners</A>||||reg||1
Z||000012||Raydar||03-21-2001||01:10 PM||||Okay, just remembered something that I saw a few years back. Was at the local Honda dealer, picking up my V-65 Sabre from having some work done. <BR>In the shop was a 900 Custom, that belonged to our local police department. After much cranking it finally chugged to life, coughing, backfiring, and belching out huge clouds of smoke. After a minute or two, it finally smoothed out and settled down to the sewing-machine idle that most Hondas have.<BR>Seems that one of the County's Finest had pulled up to the county gas island (which they share with the Road and Sewer trucks) and had topped off the tank with diesel. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/eek.gif"><BR>The bike was at the dealer to have the fuel system flushed.<BR>And they give those guys guns and badges...<P>------------------<BR>Raydar - aka Steve<P>88 T-top Formula<BR>88 soon-to-be-V6 coupe||||reg||1
